  "instance_name": "antisemitic_trope",
  "label": "Antisemitic Trope: 'Are They in the Room?'",
  "description": "This is a specific antisemitic trope that questions the presence of Jews in a given context, implying they are either not present or are being hidden. It is often used to suggest that Jews are not trustworthy or are not part of the 'mainstream' society. The text 'do you see them often? are they in the room with us now?' is a direct example of this trope.",
